  "content": {
    "id": "p5-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Each expression below can be made into a perfect square by adding a constant term. Determine the constant and then factorise the resulting expression.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p5-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$x^2+8x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Constant: $16$; $x^2+8x+16=(x+4)^2$.",
          "worked": "The constant is $\\left(\\frac82\\right)^2=16$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+8x+16&=x^2+2(x)(4)+4^2\\\\x^2+8x+16&=(x+4)^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^2-12x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Constant: $36$; $x^2-12x+36=(x-6)^2$.",
          "worked": "The constant is $\\left(\\frac{12}{2}\\right)^2=36$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2-12x+36&=x^2-2(x)(6)+6^2\\\\x^2-12x+36&=(x-6)^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$x^2+3x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Constant: $\\frac94$; $x^2+3x+\\frac94=\\left(x+\\frac32\\right)^2$.",
          "worked": "The constant is $\\left(\\frac32\\right)^2=\\frac94$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+3x+\\frac94&=x^2+2(x)\\left(\\frac32\\right)+\\left(\\frac32\\right)^2\\\\x^2+3x+\\frac94&=\\left(x+\\frac32\\right)^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$x^2-7x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Constant: $\\frac{49}{4}$; $x^2-7x+\\frac{49}{4}=\\left(x-\\frac72\\right)^2$.",
          "worked": "The constant is $\\left(\\frac72\\right)^2=\\frac{49}{4}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2-7x+\\frac{49}{4}&=x^2-2(x)\\left(\\frac72\\right)+\\left(\\frac72\\right)^2\\\\x^2-7x+\\frac{49}{4}&=\\left(x-\\frac72\\right)^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
  },
